-- A constrained declaration with no parameters whose type is a
-- function is defined, referenced and called under ONE calling convention
-- (static-dispatch-spike.md §8.1, §8.2, A.85; checker-v2.md §12.5). `h =
-- maxOf` here and in `Main`, `same = (==)` in `Main`, and `M.h` passed as a
-- value to `List.foldl` must all behave as the functions they name.
-- Expected `2`, `b`, `f`, `t`, `2`, `b`, `1`, `5`.
--
-- Oracle twin: this project with every such constant
-- eta-expanded (`h a b = maxOf a b`, `same a b = a == b`, and `M.h` the same
-- way) prints exactly the expected eight lines. A definition that takes the
-- evidence curried, `($m$0) => value`, called flat, `h(ev, 1, 2)`, would
-- build with exit 0 and print the JavaScript source text
-- `($p$1, $p$2) => Main$maxOf($m$0, $p$1, $p$2)` for `h 1 2`, and
-- `same 1 2` would print `t`.
pub maxOf : a, a -> a
    where a.compare : a, a -> Order
maxOf a b =
    if a < b then
        b

    else
        a


pub h : a, a -> a
    where a.compare : a, a -> Order
h =
    maxOf


pub blank : List a
    where a.eq : a, a -> Bool
blank =
    []
